WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:04.430
The ending of Avengers: Infinity War raised
a lot of questions for the future of the Marvel

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:09.890
Cinematic Universe, especially the fourth
Avengers movie, set to premiere in May 2019.

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:14.090
It's impossible to talk about this movie without
getting into spoilers, so if you still somehow

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:17.450
haven't seen Infinity War, we'll let Mark
Ruffalo fill you in.

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:19.960
"Wait'll you see this next one, everybody
dies."

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:20.960
"Dude!"

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:22.980
"Not everybody…"

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:27.890
Thanos' quest to retrieve the six stones of
the Infinity Gauntlet ends with fatal consequences

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:32.230
for many of Earth's mightiest heroes, with
characters being thrown off cliffs, strangled,

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:35.170
exploded, and ultimately turned into ash.

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:39.130
But as dire as the ending seems, it's unlikely
that all those dearly departed heroes will

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:43.480
stay that way for long, especially considering
many of the supposedly deceased have already

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:46.040
been confirmed to appear in Avengers 4.

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:50.170
Whether it's via flashback, time travel, or
convenient resurrection, it's clear that many

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:53.230
of our favorite fallen heroes will be returning
from the grave.

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:57.650
While the question of how remains mysterious,
here's a rundown of all the superheroes confirmed

00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:00.559
to return for Avengers 4.

00:01:00.559 --> 00:01:01.809
Ant-Man

00:01:01.809 --> 00:01:05.070
Ant-Man appears to have made it out alive
by simply not showing up.

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:08.420
After sitting out the events of Avengers:
Infinity War, Paul Rudd's Scott Lang will

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:10.850
be back in action for the fourth team-up movie.

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:15.030
As far as Black Widow knows in Infinity War,
Scott was busy caring for his family and being

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:18.039
under house arrest at the time of Thanos'
invasion.

00:01:18.039 --> 00:01:21.499
We'll learn more about where he is exactly
in Ant-Man and the Wasp, the story of which

00:01:21.499 --> 00:01:25.170
could potentially even provide a segue to
his role in Avengers 4.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:29.439
Since Rudd was spotted on the set of the team-up's
production, it's safe to say he plays at least

00:01:29.439 --> 00:01:32.270
a small part in the big story.

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:33.270
Black Panther

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:37.450
Chadwick Boseman's T'Challa was one of the
most surprising characters to bite the dust

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:38.929
at the end of Infinity War.

00:01:38.929 --> 00:01:43.299
Though his exit was shocking, Boseman's presence
on the Atlanta set for Avengers 4 suggests

00:01:43.299 --> 00:01:45.290
a relatively hasty return.

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:48.979
Considering the fact that Black Panther's
standalone film made over $1 billion at the

00:01:48.979 --> 00:01:53.539
box office and has a sequel in the works,
it seems safe to assume that the king of Wakanda

00:01:53.539 --> 00:01:57.140
will find his way back from the Necropolis
in Avengers 4.

00:01:57.140 --> 00:01:58.419
Black Widow

00:01:58.419 --> 00:02:02.479
Black Widow is one of the few characters who
survived the events of Infinity War, so it's

00:02:02.479 --> 00:02:04.770
only natural that she come back for round
two.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:07.459
And this time, she'll have a bigger role to
play.

00:02:07.459 --> 00:02:10.840
Screenwriters Christopher Markus and Stephen
McFeely have acknowledged that Black Widow

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:14.719
ends up slightly sidelined in Infinity War,
and indicated that they couldn't afford to

00:02:14.719 --> 00:02:17.290
give her as much screen time as fans might
have liked.

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:20.060
They felt comfortable pushing her into the
background because they knew there would be

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:22.980
more to come, for both her and Captain America.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:26.780
According to Markus, "We realized they had
far more potential in the movie coming next

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:31.670
year, just in terms of how their characters
would be tested by the story."

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:32.730
Captain America

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:37.090
Chris Evans has been planning his exit from
the MCU for a while now, and it's highly likely

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:40.379
that Avengers 4 will mark his swan song as
Captain America.

00:02:40.379 --> 00:02:44.099
Like Black Widow, it appears he'll have more
to do in the story in the next go-around.

00:02:44.099 --> 00:02:48.340
Intriguing set pictures not only showed Evans
on the set of the fourth movie, but also wearing

00:02:48.340 --> 00:02:50.599
his old costume from the first Avengers.

00:02:50.599 --> 00:02:53.159
From a plot standpoint, the implications are
fascinating.

00:02:53.159 --> 00:02:55.500
Are we going to see Cap get up to some time
travel?

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:59.189
Will there be two Captains Americas running
around, and the different suits are how we

00:02:59.189 --> 00:03:00.189
tell them apart?

00:03:00.189 --> 00:03:03.540
Wait, is that why Black Widow's blonde now?

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:04.739
Captain Marvel

00:03:04.739 --> 00:03:08.730
We won't get the chance to officially meet
Brie Larson's Captain Marvel until the character's

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:13.379
standalone film comes out in March 2019, but
we did get our first tease of her entry into

00:03:13.379 --> 00:03:16.709
the MCU thanks to Infinity War's post-credits
scene.

00:03:16.709 --> 00:03:20.819
Considering that so many of the MCU's other
heroes are currently out of commission, it's

00:03:20.819 --> 00:03:25.620
a sure bet that Captain Marvel will help save
the day in Avengers 4 one way or another.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:29.260
Photos reportedly from the set of the movie
revealed her sporting a green variation of

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:33.999
her costume, and Josh Brolin has said he shot
at least one scene with Larson for the Infinity

00:03:33.999 --> 00:03:36.109
War story's conclusion.

00:03:36.109 --> 00:03:37.739
Falcon

00:03:37.739 --> 00:03:41.620
Anthony Mackie's Falcon may have been snapped
out of existence in Infinity War, but he has

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:45.569
already assured fans that he'll be back for
the fourth film, sharing a picture of himself

00:03:45.569 --> 00:03:47.280
relaxing on the movie's set.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:51.180
Mackie's even gone so far as to offer up a
bit of a plot summary for fans in an interview

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:52.180
with MTV.

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:53.430
"A whole lot of people fighting.

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:54.959
A whole lot of people talking.

00:03:54.959 --> 00:03:58.670
It's a war of infinity proportions, cut the
check."

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:00.270
Gamora

00:04:00.270 --> 00:04:06.999
Gamora, played by Zoe Saldana met a particularly
tragic end in Infinity War, with Thanos sacrificing

00:04:06.999 --> 00:04:10.189
his adopted daughter in order to obtain the
Soul Stone.

00:04:10.189 --> 00:04:14.109
Considering that her demise occurred prior
to Thanos' universe-culling snap, it's a plot

00:04:14.109 --> 00:04:18.440
turn that seemed like it might stick, that
is, until Saldana appeared to say otherwise.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:22.750
Speaking to E! News, Saldana said her last
day on the set of Infinity War didn't feel

00:04:22.750 --> 00:04:24.680
like "goodbye", but "to be continued".

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:28.789
The comment seems to confirm her involvement
in the fourth film, even if it doesn't necessarily

00:04:28.789 --> 00:04:30.680
mean Gamora will be coming back to life.

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:34.490
Maybe she'll be glimpsed in flashback, or
stuck in a strange dimension inside of the

00:04:34.490 --> 00:04:35.490
Soul Stone.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:39.460
Whatever the specifics, it sure looks like
she'll be back.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:40.530
Hawkeye

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:44.990
Fans were heartbroken over the absence of
Jeremy Renner's Hawkeye from Avengers: Infinity

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:45.990
War.

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:48.340
You never know, his bow and arrow could've
made the difference.

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:52.500
Like Ant-Man, Hawkeye was said to have taken
a house arrest deal with the government following

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:56.750
the events of Captain America: Civil War,
retiring from avenging to spend time with

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:57.750
his family.

00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:00.340
But Renner has confirmed that he filmed for
Avengers 4.

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:04.500
More intriguingly, the actor was spotted on
set with a new haircut, covering up a costume

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:08.870
that looks suspiciously like the superhero
Ronin, an identity his character temporarily

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:09.950
assumed in the comics.

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:14.710
Regardless of which name he goes by, the screenwriters
have promised that Hawkeye will be a big part

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:17.949
of the fourth film, telling BuzzFeed, "We
like Hawkeye.

00:05:17.949 --> 00:05:21.910
We like Hawkeye so much we gave him a really
good story."

00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:22.910
Hulk

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:27.160
Mark Ruffalo's Bruce Banner had some performance
issues in the third Avengers movie, but at

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:28.490
least he made it out alive.

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:32.050
After spending a whole movie unable to summon
the Hulk, it seems fair to expect that his

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:35.120
powers will be returned to him at some point
in part four.

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:39.060
Ruffalo has said that Thor: Ragnarok and the
third and fourth Avengers films are designed

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:44.610
to form one Hulk storyline over three installments,
and it's a story likely to end with a bang.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:48.590
Ruffalo was also spotted on set in a motion
capture suit, so either he's still inside

00:05:48.590 --> 00:05:52.700
that Hulkbuster, or the big green guy is coming
back.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:54.000
Iron Man

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:57.569
If you believe the rumors, then Avengers 4
could be the end of Tony Stark.

00:05:57.569 --> 00:06:01.240
Although Robert Downey Jr. hasn't shared any
information on whether or not his character

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:04.970
will make it through Avengers 4, he has been
one of the more outspoken cast members when

00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:07.250
it comes to hyping the film on social media.

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:11.159
From all the photos he's shared of his involvement
in the movie's production, we know for sure

00:06:11.159 --> 00:06:12.250
that he will appear.

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:16.360
Whether he makes it out alive, well, that's
another story.

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:17.360
Mantis

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:21.470
Like most of the Guardians of the Galaxy,
Pom Klementieff's Mantis disintegrated at

00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:22.960
the end of Infinity War.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:26.200
Klementieff, though, has already seemingly
confirmed that she'll be back on board for

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:30.120
Avengers 4, sharing a photo of her make-up
trailer on social media.

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:33.530
It doesn't tell us anything about where she's
gone or how she's coming back, but it does

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:36.900
show that at least Mantis will be returning
for the next Avengers.

00:06:36.900 --> 00:06:40.720
Additionally, Chris Pratt revealed in an Instagram
post that he'll be filming Guardians of the

00:06:40.720 --> 00:06:43.280
Galaxy Vol. 3 with her in 2019.

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:47.639
It seems like Avengers 4 has no choice but
to get things back on track for the spacefaring

00:06:47.639 --> 00:06:50.939
team before their next adventure.

00:06:50.939 --> 00:06:51.939
Nebula

00:06:51.939 --> 00:06:55.840
Karen Gillan's Nebula didn't exactly have
a smooth ride through Infinity War, but she

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:58.319
was one of the few characters that survived
the trip.

00:06:58.319 --> 00:07:02.051
Not only will Nebula be back for Avengers
4, Gillan has shared a hope that her character

00:07:02.051 --> 00:07:05.250
will be able to "somehow face her daddy issues
head-on" in the film.

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:09.099
For what it's worth, Nebula was also very
important to defeating Thanos in the comic

00:07:09.099 --> 00:07:13.669
book version of the story, turning the tide
of battle by stealing the Gauntlet for herself.

00:07:13.669 --> 00:07:17.960
Whether she makes the same move in the movie
or not, Infinity War perfectly sets up Nebula's

00:07:17.960 --> 00:07:21.949
Avengers 4 arc for redemption, and revenge.

00:07:21.949 --> 00:07:22.979
Scarlet Witch

00:07:22.979 --> 00:07:26.880
Elizabeth Olsen's Scarlet Witch ended the
movie being thoroughly defeated, forced to

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:31.360
watch Vision's life end not just once, but
twice before being defeated herself.

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:35.400
Wanda is confirmed to come back to finish
the fight in Avengers 4, with Olsen sharing

00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:38.630
a pic of a bruise she received on the set
during a flying scene.

00:07:38.630 --> 00:07:42.919
Here's hoping we get to see the powerful Avenger
really unleash the chaos in the fourth movie.

00:07:42.919 --> 00:07:46.600
With the love of her life being taken out
so cruelly by Thanos, she's never had more

00:07:46.600 --> 00:07:48.720
to avenge.

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:49.830
Spider-Man

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:53.819
Tom Holland's Spider-Man had one of the most
brutal disappearing scenes in Infinity War,

00:07:53.819 --> 00:07:57.210
but it's one that has the least impact when
you know what's going on behind the scenes.

00:07:57.210 --> 00:08:00.810
We've known for some time that Holland will
be suiting up as Peter Parker again for a

00:08:00.810 --> 00:08:05.319
second standalone film, which is set to hit
theaters just a few months after Avengers

00:08:05.319 --> 00:08:06.319
4's release.

00:08:06.319 --> 00:08:10.199
We also know he's a part of Avengers 4 because
he reportedly broke his nose on the set of

00:08:10.199 --> 00:08:11.300
the production.

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:15.490
"Who said acting was easy huh?

00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:17.870
Broken nose number three.

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:19.360
What a way to finish a movie."

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:22.449
Thanos will pay for this one.

00:08:22.449 --> 00:08:23.469
Thor

00:08:23.469 --> 00:08:27.250
Chris Hemsworth's Thor spent most of Infinity
War getting back to full power, and you can

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:30.030
bet he'll put that power to good use in Avengers
4.

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:33.751
Despite the fact that the character got a
stylish haircut in Thor: Ragnarok, Hemsworth

00:08:33.751 --> 00:08:37.560
was spotted on set sporting the character's
old long-haired look, which again implies

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:42.770
either a flashback or some time travel in
store for the god of Thunder.

00:08:42.770 --> 00:08:43.770
Vision

00:08:43.770 --> 00:08:47.720
Paul Bettany's Vision got it the worst of
anyone in Infinity War, getting brutally put

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:50.210
out to pasture not just once, but twice.

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:53.790
Despite the fact that the Mind Stone that
gives him life is now embedded in Thanos'

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:57.660
Gauntlet, Bettany has confirmed that he'll
be back on board for the fourth movie.

00:08:57.660 --> 00:09:01.940
The actor shared a picture of himself in full
Vision regalia, complete with Mind Stone,

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:05.810
in late 2017, filling out paperwork on the
set of Avengers 4.

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:09.060
While it seems safe to assume that Vision
will end up having to do more than just push

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:13.570
paper around when he comes back, it remains
unclear how he'll factor into the story.

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:17.440
Maybe Shuri managed to back up his memory
after all, and he can just go back to being

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:20.010
Iron Man's butler again.

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:21.140
War Machine

00:09:21.140 --> 00:09:25.310
Don Cheadle's War Machine is one of the most
tenacious Avengers, always managing to bounce

00:09:25.310 --> 00:09:27.290
back from what looks like certain doom.

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:31.210
As one of the few survivors of Infinity War,
the Iron Man sidekick will be needed more

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:32.210
than ever.

00:09:32.210 --> 00:09:35.980
Both Josh Brolin and Gwyneth Paltrow have
said that they share scenes with Cheadle in

00:09:35.980 --> 00:09:39.220
Avengers 4, making his involvement all but
certain.

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:40.760
Thanos is still out there, after all.

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:44.670
Rhodey's gatling gun has some work left to
do.

00:09:44.670 --> 00:09:45.710
Wasp

00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:50.310
Evangeline Lilly's Hope van Dyne is finally
suiting up to headline the relatively-lighthearted

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:51.710
Ant-Man and the Wasp.

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:55.720
It's one of the two Marvel films slated to
be released between Infinity War and Avengers

00:09:55.720 --> 00:09:59.200
4, and leads up to an appearance by the Wasp
in the 2019 team-up.

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:02.890
While Lilly herself has confirmed that she'll
be a part of the fourth movie, she's also

00:10:02.890 --> 00:10:05.570
said that you shouldn't expect too much of
her in the film.

00:10:05.570 --> 00:10:09.530
According to a Q&amp;A on her Instagram page,
she's "not going to be [in it] a ton."

00:10:09.530 --> 00:10:13.250
However, she did say that she's "proud" and
"stoked" to be on board for the movie, adding

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:15.700
that she had "so much fun" on the film's set.

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:19.770
That's what happens when you show up just
in time for the happy ending.

00:10:19.770 --> 00:10:21.160
Winter Soldier

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:25.310
Sebastian Stan's Bucky Barnes has had quite
the journey in the MCU, as his friendship

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:28.730
with Steve Rogers has been tested by time,
mind control, and more.

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:32.520
While this made his last moments in Infinity
War all the more heartbreaking, neither we

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:35.250
nor Steve have seen the end of Bucky Barnes
yet.

00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:38.830
While Stan's remained tight-lipped about how
his character could be coming back, he has

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:41.290
confirmed that he filmed scenes for Avengers
4.

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:45.130
The actor has kept silent about the role he'll
play in the sequel's story, but we certainly

00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:46.520
know what we want to see.

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:50.530
If Chris Evans really is leaving after his
next movie, well, someone's gotta be around

00:10:50.530 --> 00:10:51.530
to pick up the shield.

00:10:51.530 --> 00:10:52.530
Thanks for watching!

00:10:52.530 --> 00:10:55.510
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:55.510 --> 00:10:57.700
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

